{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q137343184","formula":"C₁₃H₁₉NO₃","hill":"C13H19NO3","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":13.0,"H":19.0,"N":1.0,"O":3.0},"names":{"en":"3-methoxy-4,5-trimethylenedioxyamphetamine"},"descriptions":{"en":"MTDA, or MPDA, also known as 3-methoxy-4,5-trimethylenedioxyamphetamine or as 5-methoxy-TDA, is a chemical compound of the phenethylamine and amphetamine families related to the MDxx compounds like MDMA and the EDxx compounds like EDMA. It is the 5-methoxy derivative of 3,4-trimethylenedioxyamphetamine (TDA) and the analogue of MMDA (5-methoxy-MDA) and MEDA (5-methoxy-EDA) in which the 3,4-alkylenedioxy ring is a further-expanded 3,4-trimethylenedioxy ring. It was synthesized, tested, and described by Alexander Shulgin in his 1991 book PiHKAL (Phenethylamines I Have Known and Loved). He tested it at doses of up to 8 mg orally and observed no activity."},"fame":1,"pubchemCid":170864921,"mass":237.29,"charge":0,"smiles":"CC(CC1=CC2=C(C(=C1)OC)OCCCO2)N","inchikey":"XCXNZPQOBJFUIH-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"1-(6-methoxy-3,4-dihydro-2H-1,5-benzodioxepin-8-yl)propan-2-amine","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"rdkit","ref":"170864921","atoms":36,"license":"Computed with RDKit from SMILES (PubChem, Wikidata)"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":4.579,"y":-0.527,"z":-1.187,"el":"C"},{"x":3.315,"y":-0.289,"z":-0.358,"el":"C"},{"x":2.262,"y":0.476,"z":-1.19,"el":"C"},{"x":0.854,"y":0.344,"z":-0.652,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.052,"y":-0.539,"z":-1.25,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.352,"y":-0.678,"z":-0.755,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.776,"y":0.114,"z":0.326,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.864,"y":0.977,"z":0.961,"el":"C"},{"x":0.44,"y":1.09,"z":0.461,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.346,"y":1.689,"z":2.032,"el":"O"},{"x":-0.396,"y":2.379,"z":2.832,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.054,"y":0.091,"z":0.841,"el":"O"},{"x":-4.065,"y":-0.029,"z":-0.158,"el":"C"},{"x":